{{smaller|'''Adam’s ale.''' See ''Adam.''—'''Bitter ale, bitter beer,''' a clear, strong, highly hopped ale, of a pleasant bitter taste.—'''Medicated ale,''' ale which is prepared for medicinal purposes by an infusion of herbs during fermentation.}}

¶'''aleak''' (ạ-lēk′), ''prep. phr.'' as ''adv.'' [< ''a''<sup>3</sup> + ''leak'', q. v.] In or into a leaking state.

'''aleatico''' (al-ē-at′i-kō), ''n.'' [It.] A sweet and strong red wine made in Tuscany. {{smaller|It is of dark-red color, has a delicate flavor and perfume, and is one of the best of very sweet wines.}}

'''aleatory''' (ā′lẹ̄-ạ-tō-ri), ''a.'' [< L. ''aleatorius'', pertaining to a gamester or to gaming, < ''aleator'', a gamester, a player with dice, < ''alea'', a game with dice.] Literally, depending upon the throw of a die; hence, depending on a contingent event.—{{smaller|'''Aleatory contract,''' in ''law'', an agreement the conditions of which depend on an uncertain event.—'''Aleatory sale,''' a sale the completion of which depends on the happening of some uncertain event.}}

'''aleavement†''', ''n.'' See ''allevement''.

'''ale-bench''' (āl′bench), ''n.'' [ME. not found; < AS. ''ealu-benc'': see ''ale'' and ''bench''.] A bench in or before an ale-house.
